      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443907979,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi, \nThe purpose of the ANSI and GSM grouping in the menu is to group the statistics according to the standard defining them.\n\nIn the early days of mobile telphony US and Europe useddifferent standards ANSI in the US and ETSI GSM in Europe and\nother places in the world (this evolved into UMTS). ETSI European Telecommunications Standards Institute GSM Groupe spécial mobile (French, \"Special Mobile Group\"; official expansion is now Global System for Mobile Communications).\n\nSo perhaps trhe text should say someting like ANSI based Protocol statistics followed by the explanation of ANSI.\nSimmilarily then for GSM.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
